### Arm C: which flag actually moves arm A, debug-assertions or
###        overflow-checks. The first sets the second by default, so arm A
###        cannot tell them apart. dimension::build_profile's grammar names
###        debug-assertions and opt level and not overflow-checks, so which
###        one acts decides whether the declared axis names the thing that
###        moves or a proxy for it.
debug-assertions       overflow-checks        const-context outcome
on                     on                     REFUSED error[E0080]
on                     off                    value const 44
off                    on                     REFUSED error[E0080]
off                    off                    value const 44
### N4, the four cells must not all be the same, or the arm distinguishes
###     nothing and cannot say which flag acts.
  PASS, 2 distinct outcomes across the four cells

### Arm D: the same 2x2 on the literal-in-a-const shape the matrix used,
###        so the two shapes can be compared under one flag pair. If the
###        literal refuses in all four cells and the const fn call refuses
###        in two, the two arms are measuring different mechanisms and the
###        matrix's result does not generalise to a const fn.
debug-assertions       overflow-checks        const A: u8 = 200 + 100
on                     on                     REFUSED error[E0080]
on                     off                    REFUSED error[E0080]
off                    on                     REFUSED error[E0080]
off                    off                    REFUSED error[E0080]
### N5, arm D must differ from arm C somewhere, or the two shapes behave
###     the same and there is nothing to report.
  PASS, the two shapes disagree, so they are different mechanisms

### Arm E: the same operation written so the refusal is a value the body
###        inspects rather than a check the backend may not have emitted.
###        If this refuses in all four cells, the guarantee arm C loses is
###        recoverable by construction and the finding is constructive
###        rather than a complaint.
debug-assertions       overflow-checks        const-context outcome
on                     on                     REFUSED error[E0080]
on                     off                    REFUSED error[E0080]
off                    on                     REFUSED error[E0080]
off                    off                    REFUSED error[E0080]
### N6, arm E's control: the same body with operands that fit must produce
###     a value in all four cells, or arm E refuses for the wrong reason.
  da=on   oc=on   const 255
  da=on   oc=off  const 255
  da=off  oc=on   const 255
  da=off  oc=off  const 255
  PASS
